@startuml
' =============================================================================
' Amazon Bedrock Guardrails — evaluation of one Converse or ConverseStream request
' UML activity diagram
'
' Mermaid source set : diagrams/mermaid/18-guardrails.md (views B, C1, C2 and C3)
' Chapters           : 01-amazon-bedrock/guardrails/01-guardrails.md,
'                      01-amazon-bedrock/guardrails/02-automated-reasoning-and-enforcement.md
' Verified           : 2026-11-15
' Status             : academy design, not an official AWS reference architecture.
'                      The guardrail lane is a conceptual model of documented behaviour.
'                      No AWS icons; nothing is included from the network.
'
' Official sources this view relies on:
'   https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails-how.html
'   https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails-use-converse-api.html
'   https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails-streaming.html
'   https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails-permissions-id.html
'   https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails-enforcements.html
'   https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails-tiers.html
'   https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails-sensitive-filters.html
'   https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/monitoring-guardrails-cw-metrics.html
'   https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails-use-independent-api.html
'
' What UML adds over the Mermaid view: the three sequence views (blocked input,
' masked output, streaming) become one control flow with explicit decisions,
' and the parallel policy evaluation is a fork.
' =============================================================================
!pragma layout smetana
title Amazon Bedrock Guardrails — evaluation of one Converse or ConverseStream request (UML activity)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #333333
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #555555
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #555555
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam noteBorderColor #888888
skinparam legendBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam legendBorderColor #888888

|#FFFBF5|Your application\nexecution role|
start
:Converse or ConverseStream with guardrailConfig
(guardrail ID, numbered version, trace)
TLS · SigV4; <<#FDEBD0>>

|#F5FBF6|Amazon Bedrock Runtime\nguardrail evaluation and model invocation|
:Authorize bedrock:InvokeModel and bedrock:ApplyGuardrail
IAM identity policy and SCP · bedrock:GuardrailIdentifier; <<#FDECEA>>
if (Allowed?) then (no)
  :AccessDeniedException
  (for example the role names another guardrail than its IAM deny allows); <<#FDECEA>>
  stop
else (yes)
endif

:Collect the applicable guardrails
request guardrail (pinned version)
+ account-level enforced guardrail configuration
+ organisation guardrail from the BEDROCK_POLICY; <<#FDECEA>>
note right
  The effect is the union of every applicable guardrail.
  Standard tier: evaluation can be routed to destination Regions
  of the guardrail profile in the same geography
end note
:Select the input to assess
only guardContent blocks, if any exist; <<#FDECEA>>
fork
  :Content filters
  text and image · prompt attacks; <<#FDECEA>>
fork again
  :Denied topics; <<#FDECEA>>
fork again
  :Word filters; <<#FDECEA>>
fork again
  :Sensitive information filters; <<#FDECEA>>
fork again
  :Other configured policies; <<#FDECEA>>
end fork
note right
  Input is evaluated first, in parallel
  for each configured policy
end note

if (Any policy action BLOCKED on the input?) then (yes)
  |Amazon Bedrock Runtime\nguardrail evaluation and model invocation|
  :Model not called
  (documented: the foundation model inference is discarded); <<#E6F4EA>>
  :Return the blocked-input message
  stopReason guardrail_intervened · usage 0 tokens in the documented example; <<#E6F4EA>>
else (no)
  |Amazon Bedrock Runtime\nguardrail evaluation and model invocation|
  :Invoke the foundation model; <<#E6F4EA>>
    :Foundation model generates the output; <<#E6F4EA>>
  |Amazon Bedrock Runtime\nguardrail evaluation and model invocation|
  if (ConverseStream with streamProcessingMode async?) then (yes)
    :Release contentBlockDelta chunks at once; <<#E6F4EA>>
        :Assess the output in the background; <<#FDECEA>>
    note right
      Chunks may contain inappropriate content until the scan completes.
      After a violation, later chunks are blocked.
      Sensitive information cannot be masked in this mode
    end note
  else (no: Converse, or sync streaming — the default)
        :Assess the output
    (streaming: buffered chunks before release); <<#FDECEA>>
    if (Action on the output?) then (BLOCKED)
      :Replace the answer with the blocked-output message; <<#FDECEA>>
    elseif (ANONYMIZED) then
      :Replace sensitive values with placeholders; <<#FDECEA>>
      note right
        Same stopReason as a block: guardrail_intervened.
        The trace shows action ANONYMIZED and still
        holds the unmasked value — do not log it
      end note
    else (none)
      :Leave the answer unchanged; <<#E6F4EA>>
    endif
  endif
  |Amazon Bedrock Runtime\nguardrail evaluation and model invocation|
  :Return the answer, masked answer or message
  trace in the response (metadata event when streaming); <<#E6F4EA>>
endif

|Amazon Bedrock Runtime\nguardrail evaluation and model invocation|
fork
  :Metrics in AWS/Bedrock/Guardrails
  InvocationsIntervened · InvocationThrottles · FindingCounts; <<#FFF8E1>>
fork again
  :CloudTrail data event for ApplyGuardrail
  (when the trail selects guardrail data events); <<#FFF8E1>>
fork again
  :Model invocation log record (when enabled)
  blocked content in plain text · masking does not apply; <<#FFF8E1>>
end fork

|Your application\nexecution role|
:Read stopReason and the trace action; <<#FDEBD0>>
stop

floating note left
  Not assessed by the guardrail: toolResult blocks,
  tool definitions and toolUse.input. Add ApplyGuardrail
  on tool output. ApplyGuardrail alone (source INPUT
  or OUTPUT) works for any model, including models
  outside Amazon Bedrock. No guardrail on bedrock-mantle.
end note

legend right
  |= Notation |= Meaning |
  | swimlane | who performs the action (red actions: guardrail evaluation) |
  | fork bar | actions that run in parallel |
  | diamond | decision on documented behaviour |
  |<#FDEBD0> orange | your compute |
  |<#E6F4EA> green | Amazon Bedrock and the model |
  |<#FDECEA> red | security control or denial |
  |<#FFF8E1> yellow | telemetry and audit record |
  Academy design · not an official AWS diagram · Verified 2026-11-15
endlegend
@enduml
